## for loop
A `for` loop combines three things in one line: init, condition, and update.

```qc
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    println(i);
}
// 0
// 1
// 2
// 3
// 4
```

Breaking it down:
- `int i = 0` - runs once at the start
- `i < 5` - checked before each loop, stops when false
- `i++` - runs after each loop

### Compared to while:
```qc
// these do the same thing
int i = 0;
while (i < 5) {
    println(i);
    i++;
}

for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    println(i);
}
```

`for` is cleaner when you know how many times to loop.


